            <ArticleTitle>Perhexiline maleate as a cause of reversible parkinsonism and peripheral neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a 78-year-old woman receiving perhexiline maleate for intractable angina pectoris, a syndrome of parkinsonism and peripheral neuropathy developed. The neuropathy was confirmed by electromyographic and nerve conduction studies. The parkinsonism and peripheral neuropathy disappeared when perhexiline maleate was discontinued.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
